<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/associate-professor-ceridwen-owen-8e9e109d38f0> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Associate Professor Ceridwen Owen"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-architecture-and-design-34d92f346705> ;
    utas:bio "Ceridwen is an Associate Professor in Architecture & Design at the University of Tasmania where she co-leads the Diverse Inclusions Lab. She is also a founding Partner of Core Collective Architects with whom she collaborates on pro-bono and research-in-practice projects.Ceridwen's research centres on design for health, social inclusion and sustainability with a particular emphasis on cognitive and sensory diversity and trauma-informed design. She has led and contributed to numerous multi-disciplinary research projects exploring how environments can be designed to be more inclusive and enabling. This has included research into independent, supported and crisis accommodation, early childhood, primary and tertiary education environments, and playspaces.Participation and inclusion are central to Ceridwen’s research. She works collaboratively with academics and practitioners across diverse disciplines, and employs creative research methods to broaden participation and foreground lived‑experience perspectives. Alongside traditional academic publications, she undertakes translational research through built projects and design guidelines.Ceridwen completed her architectural qualifications at the Edinburgh College of Art (1st Class Hons 1991) and the Mackintosh School in Glasgow (Postgraduate Diploma 1993). After moving to Australia she worked in practice for several years in the area of sustainable architecture before commencing her Doctorate at the University of Melbourne in 1999. Following the completion of her Doctorate, Ceridwen joined the University of Tasmania in 2005.Career summaryQualificationsPh.D.; The Green Field: the sub-culture of sustainable architecture, University of Melbourne, Australia 2004DipArch; Mackintosh School of Architecture/Glasgow University, Scotland 1993BArch (Hons First Class); Edinburgh College of Art/Heriot-Watt University, Scotland 1991MembershipsProfessional practice2023 - Australian Institute of Architecture (AIA) - Continuing Professional Development Committee (Tasmania)2015 - 2017: Australian Institute of Architects (AIA) – Education Committee (Tasmania)2014 – 2018: Honorary Secretary, Association of Architecture Schools Australasia2012: Chair, AIA Tasmanian State Architecture Awards Juror2011 - : Representative on Visiting Panels for accreditation of architecture programs2008 - 2010: AIA Chapter Council Member (Tasmanian Chapter)2007 - 2011: Architects for Peace, Editor, AFP Editorials2005 - 2015: Australian Institute of Architects – Sustainability Committee (Tasmania)1999 - : Architects Registration Board (Victoria and Tasmania – registered architect) Communities of Practice (UTAS) Trauma-informed Practice Education for Sustainability Administrative expertise Ceridwen has worked in a number of senior leadership roles in the University including Acting Head of School, Deputy Head of School, Program Director Architecture and Course Coordinator for the Bachelor of Design. She also co-established and ran an architectural practice, Core Collective Architects. She currently leads the Research in Practice portfolio in the School of Architecture & Design."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Associate Professor Ceridwen Owen"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Ceridwen.Owen"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Ceridwen.Owen"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Ceridwen.Owen@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
