<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/associate-professor-erin-roehrer-2c48b9c9e012> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Associate Professor Erin Roehrer"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Associate Professor Erin Roehrer is a member of the School of Information and Communication Technology at the University of Tasmania. She is a leader in designing, delivering, and advancing technology‑enhanced learning that supports diverse learners and drives innovation across transnational education contexts. A Fellow of the Higher Education Academy, Erin brings a collaborative and reflective teaching philosophy that empowers both students and colleagues. She has led major curriculum renewals, received multiple learning and teaching awards, and serves as Associate Editor for Australia’s highest‑impact education journal, the Journal of University Teaching and Learning Practice. Erin is a values‑driven academic leader who embodies a “leading from within and alongside” philosophy in every role. She has held a range of leadership positions and is currently Deputy Chair of Academic Senate, Chair of the Curriculum Quality Assurance Committee (CQAC), and Associate Head Students (School of ICT). In these roles, Erin shapes inclusive student experiences, supports staff development, and champions academic excellence through collaborative, context‑aware leadership across local, national, and international partnerships. In 2024, Erin received a Vice‑Chancellor’s Citation for Outstanding Contributions to Student Learning, recognising her transformative impact across transnational and local learning environments. She has also been awarded three Teaching Merit Certificates (2013, 2016, 2022), a team Vice‑Chancellor’s Award (2015), and numerous Unit Commendations from students. Her work is consistently commended for fostering engaging, inclusive, and high‑quality learning experiences that respond to diverse student and contextual needs. Erin’s leadership is defined not only by her own achievements but by her commitment to enabling others to thrive. She has mentored colleagues across disciplines and academic levels, many of whom have progressed to promotion, secured awards, or led impactful learning and teaching initiatives. Her influence extends nationally through editorial and scholarly contributions, and institutionally through strategic leadership roles that shape governance, curriculum renewal, and student engagement. Her work exemplifies a values‑led, collaborative approach to academic leadership, grounded in trust, inclusivity, and a sustained commitment to learning and teaching excellence."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Associate Professor Erin Roehrer"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Erin.Roehrer"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Erin.Roehrer"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Erin.Roehrer@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
