<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/associate-professor-hossein-enshaei-eddffcad9ba2> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Associate Professor Hossein Enshaei"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/australian-maritime-college-b2b959211c61> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Hossein Enshaei interest is in the field of marine technologies.Hossein commenced his career as a seafarer and has 13 years of service as a navigator on ocean going vessels. He left the sea in 1999 while he was a Master mariner to join the training institute to train seafarer and served as a lecturer and head of deck department. Upon his graduation as a naval architect in 2004, he joined shipbuilding industry and completed three unique projects. Hossein pursued his career as a maritime researcher at Newcastle University in UK while completing his PhD and served as a researcher over several national, regional and international projects while contributing to the teaching of undergraduate and postgraduate engineering programs. Since joining Australian Maritime College (AMC) in 2014, Hossein actively engaged in multidisciplinary research focusing on ship operations, developing advanced modelling, control and optimisation algorithms, and applying them to study ship’s stability and shipboard powering systems. He collaborates with individuals from different hierarchical levels and disciplines within and outside the university to enhance areas of research excellence and attract the best students and researchers from around the world. Hossein established and led a unique Real-Time Power Systems Simulator (RTPSS) facility in AMC for designing digital-twin for existing and future marine vehicles and autonomous AUVs. RTPSS not only complements existing internationally recognised AMC hydrodynamics, fluid mechanics and AUV facilities, but adds a state-of-the-art sovereign capability to Australian Maritime industry. Hossein's research interests are in ship's dynamic stability and marine informatics. He performs advanced research on ship systems, and develops decision making tools using mathematical modelling, simulation and optimisation techniques."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Associate Professor Hossein Enshaei"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Hossein.Enshaei"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Hossein.Enshaei"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Hossein.Enshaei@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/engineering-8c85b6639e62>,
