<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/associate-professor-ivona-mladineo-ab2337be2f6e> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Associate Professor Ivona Mladineo"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/institute-for-marine-and-antarctic-studies-bd99c2807811> ;
    utas:bio "Associate Professor Ivona Mladineo is an internationally recognised aquatic animal health and parasitology researcher whose work focuses on fish and invertebrate diseases, host–parasite interactions, and health management in aquaculture. She has made significant contributions to understanding marine parasites, particularly zoonotic nematodes such as Anisakis, and the impacts of pathogens on fish health, aquaculture sustainability, and food safety. Her research spans parasitology, disease ecology, functional biology, and the development of innovative approaches to aquatic animal health and disease control. With an extensive publication record and a strong international research profile, Ivona has led and contributed to numerous multidisciplinary projects addressing emerging challenges in aquaculture, climate change, aquatic biosecurity, and pathogen management. She currently serves as Associate Professor in Aquatic Animal Health at the University of Tasmania and continues to collaborate widely with academic, government, and industry partners to advance sustainable aquatic animal production and ecosystem health."^^xsd:string ;
