    utas:bio "Nathan completed his BSc Hons in 2003 at the University of Queensland, and his PhD in 2008 at the Australian National University. He was awarded a Royal Commission for the Exhibition of 1851 Science Research Fellowship (2008-2010) at the University of Oxford (United Kingdom) and was subsequently awarded an Alexander von Humboldt Research Fellowship (2011-2013) at the Philipps-Universität Marburg (Germany). He commenced as Lecturer in Synthetic Chemistry at the University of Tasmania in 2013, and previously held a Discovery Early Career Researcher Award Fellowship (2015-2018).Career summaryQualificationsGradCert ULT University of Tasmania Australia 08/2015PhD Chiral Arsenium-Phosphine Complexes Australian National University Australia 18/07/2008BSc (1st Class Hons) University of Queensland Australia 12/2003BSc University of Queensland Australia 12/2002MembershipsProfessional practice Royal Australian Chemical Institute – Chartered Chemist Royal Australian Chemical Institute – Tasmanian Branch Committee Member Society of Crystallographers in Australia and New Zealand Australian Association of von Humboldt Fellows"^^xsd:string ;
