<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-allison-matthews-2c7e7c13c281> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Allison Matthews"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Matthews is a senior Lecturer within the School of Psychological Sciences and the Course Coordinator for the Honours program in Psychology (M4Y). Allison's research focuses on neural correlates of cognitive processes such as attention, including the role of attention in fear and anxiety, substance use, and reading ability, and the effects of meditation, nature, substances and other interventions on cognition and wellbeing. Allison also has a research interest in online, mobile and virtual reality interventions for mental health.Allison has supervised multiple PhD, Masters and Honours students across a range of research areas and is available to supervise PhD projects which align with her research interests."^^xsd:string ;
