<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-annie-foppert-6901a7231900> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Annie Foppert"@en ;
    utas:bio "The circulation of the Southern Ocean has an outsized role in global climate by controlling how heat makes its way towards the Antarctic continent and how much anthropogenic heat and carbon are stored away in the abyssal ocean. I use a suite of observational data to better understand the mechanisms for transporting heat across the Southern Ocean, where and how those warm waters get onto the Antarctic continental shelf, and what is responsible for changes in the deepest, densest waters in the ocean."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Annie Foppert"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Annie.Foppert"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Annie.Foppert"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Annie.Foppert@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/climate-change-processes-925773eaa013>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/climate-change-science-983bbbbe676a>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/earth-sciences-32a57b471aa6>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/oceanography-b86fff6aa227>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/physical-oceanography-676f77eb4c10> ;
    utas:orcid "0000-0003-2958-1454"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:researchFieldsText "Physical oceanography; Climate change processes; Climate change science; Oceanography; Earth sciences"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:supervises <https://example.org/utas-research/project/12367> ;
    utas:title "Doctor"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:updatedWhen "2026-09-16T05:48:29.0928820+10:00"^^xsd:string .

<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-anya-daly-22e57659498e> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Anya Daly"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-humanities-873a000cedf1> ;
    utas:bio "Anya is Senior Lecturer in Philosophy and Ethics in the School of Humanities, University of Tasmania. Interdisciplinary collaborations are at the core of Anya’s research interests. She investigates the intersections of phenomenology with philosophy of mind, the philosophy of perception, the philosophy of psychiatry, embodied and social cognition, enactivism, ethics, aesthetics and Buddhist Philosophy. Anya has received funding from national and international institutions to support her research projects and also to facilitate the dissemination of her own work and the work of others through publications, organising workshops and conferences. Notable among these was The Inhuman Gaze, a three-day multi-disciplinary international conference spanning the disciplines of philosophy, cognitive neuroscience, psychiatry, psychology, sociology and aesthetics, which was hosted in Paris 2018 - https://theinhumangaze.com/. Papers from this conference were published by Routledge in an edited volume for which she was the chief editor. https://www.taylorfrancis.com/books/edit/10.4324/9780367815707/perception-inhuman-gaze-dermot-moran-fred-cummins-anya-daly-james-jardineShe has published in ethics, aesthetics, philosophy of psychiatry, feminism, social cognition, philosophy of psychology, philosophy of perception, ontology and animal ethics.Anya completed a double-badged doctorate (en-cotutelle) between Université de Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne et University of Melbourne in December 2012.She has taught in programs at undergraduate and graduate levels at the University of Melbourne, Sciences Po Paris, ESSEC Paris, University Lyon 3, University College Dublin, Monash University - European philosophy, Anglo-American philosophy, history of ideas, epistemology, metaphysics, ethics, business ethics, management ethics, aesthetics, history and philosophy of psychiatry, and philosophy of science.Anya spent five years researching and teaching in France (2005-2010) under the supervision of Professor Renaud Barbaras, and two years in Dublin at University College Dublin under the mentorship of Professor Dermot Moran, on an Irish Research Council Fellowship (2016-2018). In the years 2010 - 2016, and 2018 - 2021 she was based at the University of Melbourne. Now she is based at the University of Tasmania at the Inveresk campus."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Anya Daly"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Anya.Daly"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Anya.Daly"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Anya.Daly@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/history-and-philosophy-of-specific-fields-0de2608995e6>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/history-of-ideas-afb4a6451a11>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/phenomenology-9e53c1fab6d4>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/philosophical-psychology-incl-moral-psychology-and-philosophy-of-action-8fab5a3648a3>,
