<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-benjamin-millar-8bd88f5a2b04> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Benjamin Millar"@en ;
    utas:bio "Ben has been working in Engineering Education for approximately 7 years, after completing his PhD in Electrical Engineering (power distribution optimisation). Since beginning in a teaching-intensive role at the University of Tasmania, Ben has supervised over 40 Engineering honours and masters students, and coordinated both the bachelors and masters Electronics and Communications specialisations. Ben has been active in curriculum development and has played a valuable role in the review and development of both Electronics and Electrical engineering units. Ben’s teaching is focused on electronics, embedded systems and software engineering, all critical aspects of the modern Electrical Engineering specialisation. Ben’s research has generally been focused on the application of computer systems to solving problems in renewable power systems, which aligns well with the newly introduced “Climate Safe Engineering” focus of the school in both curriculum and research. Ben has also recently increased his focus on engineering education, including supervision of a PhD candidate studying the mental models of students as they learn to programme."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Benjamin Millar"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Benjamin.Millar"^^xsd:string ;
