<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-bennet-mccomish-59d292bcda91> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Bennet McComish"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/menzies-institute-for-medical-research-12e6f452c508> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Bennet McComish is a Senior Research Fellow in the Menzies Institute for Medical Research at the University of Tasmania. He leads the Evolutionary Medicine group within the MS Research Flagship.Bennet's background is in molecular evolution and bioinformatics, and he currently leads a team investigating the evolutionary origins of genetic risk factors for multiple sclerosis. This work includes scanning human genome data for signatures of natural selection (including local adaptation) and modeling evolutionary processes such as admixture and genetic drift. He has worked across a range of complex diseases, including multiple sclerosis and inherited eye diseases. He manages a dedicated genomics high-performance computing cluster, supporting and training research staff and students who use the cluster. His work involves analysing genome sequence data using bioinformatic tools to identify the genetic variants that are most likely to be involved in causing disease.Bennet completed a PhD in Computational Biology in the Allan Wilson Centre for Molecular Ecology and Evolution (New Zealand). He joined the School of Mathematics and Physics at the University of Tasmania in 2013 as a postdoctoral researcher investigating the evolutionary dynamics of microsatellite sequences, before moving to his current position at the Menzies in 2016."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Bennet McComish"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Bennet.McComish"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Bennet.McComish"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Bennet.McComish@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/biological-sciences-4ef09db1f95d>,
