<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-elly-quinlan-08ff9e777137> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Elly Quinlan"@en ;
    utas:bio "I'm a psychologist (clinical, educational & developmental), senior lecturer, and supervisor with a focus on professional training, ethics, and inclusive practice. I've contributed to the development and review of postgraduate psychology programs across several institutions. I teach into postgraduate psychology, supervise both research and clinical placements, and support students as they navigate the realities of becoming a psychologist. I particularly value working closely with students as they develop their professional identity and confidence. My research focuses on strengthening the structures and supports that shape postgraduate psychology training and professional practice. I've explored areas such as practicum logbooks, sexual abuse inquiry, fostering tolerance of uncertainty, supporting students experiencing competency issues, and the development of mentoring programs. I also have research interests in neurodiversity and neurodivergence, role-play and gaming, recovery-oriented approaches, and the experiences of mental health carers.A consistent focus of my work is translating research into practical resources and guidance that can be used in training and professional settings. Clinically, I have worked with young people experiencing trauma, attachment disruptions, grief and loss, sexual abuse, disability, and neurodivergence, and I am particularly committed to neuroaffirming and trauma-informed approaches. Outside the university, I serve as Deputy Chair of the Psychology Board of Australia’s Registration and Compliance Committee, am a member of the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council Stakeholder Reference Group, and serve as Associate Editor of Australian Psychologist.. I also work as a Witness Intermediary in the Tasmanian justice system, supporting vulnerable witnesses to participate fairly in legal proceedings. As a neurodivergent person, I'm particularly attuned to the ways systems can either support or exclude- and I'm committed to building professional spaces that are more transparent, inclusive, and compassionate.I supervise research at the Masters and PhD level and welcome discussions with potential research candidates."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Elly Quinlan"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Elly.Quinlan"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Elly.Quinlan"^^xsd:string ;
