<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-gabi-mocatta-d038b35156d7> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Gabi Mocatta"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Gabi Mocatta is a communication and journalism researcher who currently studies communicational responses to climate change. This multifocal work takes place at the site where climate change science, public understanding and collective discourse on climate change and environmental policy intersect. Gabi also examines media representations of climate change - given most people derive their understanding of our changing climate from the media. She additionally researches climate literacy, to better understand what spurs climate action at all levels of society. Gabi is currently Senior Research Fellow in Climate Science Communication with the globally-known Climate Futures Research Group in the School of Geography, Planning and Spatial Sciences.A former journalist, Gabi began her academic career at the University of Tasmania teaching journalism. She undertook her PhD in environmental communication at the university's Media School. Gabi then worked as Lecturer in Communication and Course Director of the Masters in Communication at Deakin University, Melbourne. She has been a member of the Climate Futures research group since 2020, bringing expertise in climate communication and climate science translation for public policy making and behaviour change. Climate Futures works with with a wide range of industry and government stakeholders to deliver climate information for preparedness and adaptation.Gabi collaborates on several projects related to promoting climate literacy and action. She has worked with local government to understand and deliver climate projection needs, and to provide climate science translation for community. She also investigates the role of communication in responding to natural hazards and is a research leader for Natural Hazards Research Australia. She is also part of the team that delivers the award winning Curious Climate Schools climate literacy program for young people. Internationally, Gabi collaborates with the Media and Climate Change Observatory at the University of Colorado, Boulder, as part of the team led by Prof. Max Boykoff. This project traces media coverage of climate change around the world since 2000. She has been president of the International Environmental Communication Association (2023-2025) and in 2025 she was elected as vice-Chair, progressing to Chair, of the International Communication Association's Environmental Communication Division. Gabi is an Associate Deputy Editor of the journal Climatic Change. Prizes and Awards:2001-2003 University of Melbourne International Scholarship2013-2016 University of Tasmania Elite Scholarship2018 University of Tasmania Teaching Excellence Award2020 Commendation for Service Excellence to College of Science and Engineering as part of the Climate Futures research program2021 Deakin University Teaching and Learning Award for Curriculum Design that is Innovative, Motivates and Inspires 2022 IAMCR Climate Communication Research Fellowship Award 2022 US National Communication Association Steve E. Depoe Award for Best Book Chapter in Environmental Communication2022 Green Gowns Australasia Award for Benefitting Society as part of the Curious Climate Team2022 Vice Chancellor's Award for Engagement as part of the Curious Climate Team 2023 Highly Commended, Green Gowns International Awards for Benefitting Society as part of Curious Climate Schools team 2023 Australian Financial Review Higher Education Awards Community Engagement Award as part of Curious Climate Schools team2024/2025 Fulbright Fellowship at George Mason Center for Climate Change Communication and Department of Environmental Studies, University of Colorado Boulder 2025 Vice Chancellor's Interdisciplinary Excellence Award as part of Curious Climate Schools Team 2025 Vice Chancellor's Early Career Researcher Award 2025/2026 Natural Hazards Research Australia's ECR Fellowship"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Gabi Mocatta"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Gabi.Mocatta"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Gabi.Mocatta"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Gabi.Mocatta@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/climate-change-impacts-and-adaptation-f83eec5688b6>,
