<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-graeme-miles-1c27133987c9> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Graeme Miles"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-humanities-873a000cedf1> ;
    utas:bio "Graeme Miles is a Senior Lecturer in Classics in History & Classics in the School of Humanities and researches Greek literature (especially of the Roman Era) and philosophy (especially the Platonic tradition). In both of these broad areas he has published many studies and translations of foundational texts. He is also a publishing poet and was elected as a fellow of the Australian Academy of the Humanities in 2024.BiographyGraeme completed his undergraduate study and PhD at the University of Western Australia. Following his doctorate he was an Asialink writer in residence based at the University of Madras, then a postdoctoral research fellow at the University of Ghent, Belgium (2007), before returning to teach at UWA in early 2008. He moved to the University of Tasmania in second semester 2008.Career summaryQualificationsPhD Humanity, Animality and Divinity in Philostratus' Life of Apollonius and Heroicus University of Western Australia Australia 2007BA (Hons) Some Aspects of Euripides' Dionysus University Western Australia Australia 2000Languages (other than English)High proficiency in Ancient Greek and Latin. Reading knowledge of French, German, Italian.MembershipsProfessional practiceAustralasian Society for Classical StudiesInternational Society for Neoplatonic Studies"^^xsd:string ;
