<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-james-montgomery-cd8960f71e67> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor James Montgomery"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-information-and-communication-technology-bb00fdcb9d1d> ;
    utas:bio "James Montgomery is a senior lecturer in the School of Information & Communication Technology, based at the Sandy Bay campus. His primary research interest is in heuristic optimisation, including evolutionary computation. He also works in ecoacoustics, the use of sound to observe the environment, and is running a citizen science project named Birdsong where members of public can identify birds from their calls.James joined the University of Tasmania as Lecturer in ICT in January 2014. Prior to this he was a research fellow at Australian National University (ANU) (based at National ICT Australia's (NICTA) [now part of CSIRO] Canberra Research Laboratory), designing and implementing a general purpose web API for delivering machine learning services; a postdoctoral researcher at Swinburne University of Technology, working on external projects in data analysis and his own research in evolutionary computation; and a student and sessional lecturer at Bond University.Administrative rolesJames is currently an academic integrity advisor in the School of ICT and College of Sciences and Engineering (CoSE) representative on the Technology Enhanced Learning and Teaching Governance Group (since 2022). He was also President (2020–22) and now Treasurer of the University Club, the de facto staff club located on the Sandy Bay Campus: https://www.utas.edu.au/campuses/university-clubPreviously James was an elected member of Academic Senate from CoSE 2018–2021 and member of the University Learning and Teaching Committee 2019–2021. From 2014 to 2016 he was Hobart site coordinator for ACM International Collegiate Programming Contest, and has previously served as the recruitment and outreach lead for ICT."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor James Montgomery"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "James.Montgomery"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/James.Montgomery"^^xsd:string ;
