<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-jessica-fletcher-e2d931c5d65c> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Jessica Fletcher"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/menzies-institute-for-medical-research-12e6f452c508> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Jessica Fletcher leads the Glial Cell Signalling Research Group within the Multiple Sclerosis (MS) Research Flagship at the Menzies Institute for Medical Research. Dr Fletcher’s research focus is on understanding the contribution non-neuronal cells of the brain (called glia) make to the neurodegeneration that causes progressive disability in MS. The ultimate goal of their research is to apply this understanding to create new brain repair therapies that can be used to improve the lives of people with MS."^^xsd:string ;
