<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-luca-magri-f7050ec8fdf0> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Luca Magri"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Luca is a marine geoscientist. He completed a Bachelor of Geological Sciences at the Università degli Studi di Pavia, followed by a Master of Geology and Land Management at Alma Mater Studiorum – Università di Bologna. He obtained his PhD from the Institute for Marine and Antarctic Studies (IMAS) at the University of Tasmania, where his research investigated the post-emplacement rifting of oceanic Large Igneous Provinces. In 2024, Luca joined the EarthByte Group at the University of Sydney as a Postdoctoral Fellow, working on the tectonic evolution of the Coral Sea and the development of global datasets for the validation of palaeo-elevation reconstructions. He subsequently joined IMAS as a Research Associate, where he focuses on marine and Antarctic geophysics. Luca's research interests focus predominantly on marine geophysics, plate tectonics, ocean basin evolution, scientific ocean drilling, geodynamics, and sedimentology. His work integrates geological observations, marine geophysical data, and numerical modelling to investigate the processes that control lithospheric deformation and breakup, and the evolution of ocean basins. He has participated in several oceanographic expeditions, including IODP Expedition 402 (Tyrrhenian Continent-Ocean Transition) aboard the JOIDES Resolution in the Mediterranean Sea, as well as research voyages on RV Investigator and RV Falkor in the Southern Ocean, Southwest Pacific, and Coral Sea."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Luca Magri"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Luca.Magri"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Luca.Magri"^^xsd:string ;
