<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-mohammed-sedeeq-8fc6396f664e> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Mohammed Sedeeq"@en ;
    utas:bio "Mohammed Sedeeq is an accomplished healthcare professional with seven years of experience as a hospital pharmacist. His academic journey brought him to Australia, where he obtained a Master of Pharmaceutical Science degree from the University of Tasmania. While pursuing his education, Mohammed actively engaged in mentoring and guiding students as a tutor for the M7E Master of Pharmaceutical Science program, dedicated to enhancing their learning experiences.Mohammed Sedeeq commenced his doctoral studies with the University of Tasmania in 2019 focused Identification and characterization of novel therapeutic targets for the control of pediatric brain cancers. Mohammed's PhD research resulted in the publication of many articles and formed the basis for a successful grant application titled \"Repurposing of FDA-approved drugs against medulloblastoma\" in 2021. His research expertise encompasses the development of high-throughput screening assays, the investigation of metastatic-associated processes, and the study of calcium signaling.In 2023, Mohammed joined the University of Tasmania as a Lecturer in Pharmaceutical Science, where he taught and coordinated various academic units across both undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Mohammed Sedeeq's research interests include developing high-throughput screening assays using reporter cell lines to investigate cellular stress signaling mechanisms."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Mohammed Sedeeq"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Mohammed.Sedeeq"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Mohammed.Sedeeq"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Mohammed.Sedeeq@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/biochemistry-and-cell-biology-73298987c0e5>,
