<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-ruth-sharples-5375104d4475> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Ruth Sharples"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/institute-for-marine-and-antarctic-studies-bd99c2807811> ;
    utas:bio "I am a marine scientist specialising in fisheries assessment, population ecology, and spatial data analysis. My current work at the Institute for Marine and Antarctic Studies (IMAS), University of Tasmania, focuses on assessing the status of key Tasmanian fisheries—including scalefish, Southern Calamari, and Pale Octopus—using analytical, model-based, and empirical approaches to evaluate stock trends, fishing pressure, and sustainability. I routinely provide science-based advice to government and industry through technical reports, working groups, and briefings. My expertise spans stock assessment methods including CPUE standardization, surplus production models (CMSY, BSM, OCOM), and statistical modelling using GAMs and GLMs. I am highly proficient in R programming for data analysis and visualization, and experienced with GIS platforms (ArcGIS, QGIS) for spatial analysis of marine populations and fisheries. My earlier career centered on marine vertebrate ecology, particularly the movements, habitat use, and population dynamics of seals and seabirds in relation to offshore energy infrastructure. This research, developed through positions at world-class institutions including the Sea Mammal Research Unit (University of St Andrews), CSIRO Oceans and Atmosphere, and IMAS, provides a strong foundation for understanding fish population dynamics within broader ecosystem contexts. Across academic, government, and consultancy roles, I have developed broad expertise in species distribution modelling, satellite telemetry, and the integration of ecological and human-use datasets. I am committed to producing clear, defensible science that supports evidence-based management of marine resources and contributes to improved understanding of marine ecosystems."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Ruth Sharples"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Ruth.Sharples"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Ruth.Sharples"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Ruth.Sharples@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
