    utas:bio "Dr Tessa Vance works in the field of Palaeoclimatology, which seeks to define past climate variability and change to contextualise future climate changeBiographyTessa is a Senior Research Associate with the Australian Antarctic Program Partnership and a member of the Centre for Water, Climate and Land, based at the University of Newcastle. Career summaryTessa was previously a research associate with the Antarctic Climate and Ecosystems Cooperative Research Centre (2010-2019) and the Antarctic Gateway Program (2019-2020).Qualifications PhD - Southern Cross University (2009) BSc - James Cook University (2001)MembershipsCommittee associations American Geophysical Union (AGU) Australian Meteorological and Oceanographic Society (AMOS) European Geophysical Union (EGU)"^^xsd:string ;
