<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-til-baalisampang-0c906540f684> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Til Baalisampang"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/australian-maritime-college-b2b959211c61> ;
    utas:bio "Dr. Til Baalisampang is a senior lecturer and researcher specialising in Maritime Systems and Safety Engineering at the Australian Maritime College (AMC), University of Tasmania. He actively works for the Maritime Infrastructure Integrity and Environment (MarIInE) Laboratory, which enables the assessment of the structural integrity of maritime assets and their relationship and impacts on the marine environment. With over five years of academic experience, Dr. Baalisampang has made impactful contributions to the field through his teaching and extensive research.Dr. Baalisampang holds a PhD in Maritime Engineering from the University of Tasmania (2019). He also completed a Bachelor of Engineering (Marine & Offshore Engineering) with Honors from the same institution in 2014. Before migrating to Australia, he completed a Bachelor of Science (2006) from the University of North Bengal, India, recognised as equivalent to an Australian Bachelor of Science by the Australian Overseas Qualification Authority. Since July 2019, Dr. Baalisampang has been a lecturer at the AMC, where he is responsible for delivering Thermal Engineering, Design of Offshore Systems, Special Topics in Ocean Engineering, and Management of Engineering Projects. He is also supervising several PhD students, focusing on the safety and sustainability of offshore systems, including renewable energy systems and hydrogen. His earlier roles include a sessional lecturer and tutor, as well as a final year research mentor at the AMC, where he provided critical guidance and support to undergraduate and postgraduate students.Dr. Baalisampang has an impressive portfolio of research, with numerous publications in high-impact journals. His work primarily focuses on the safety and risk assessment of offshore and marine engineering systems. Notable publications include studies on fire impact assessment in FLNG processing facilities, LNG spill dispersion, drag reduction, hydrogen safety, and safety evaluations in maritime transportation. In addition to his academic roles, Dr. Baalisampang has international research experience, including a six-month internship at the Centre for Risk Integrity and Safety Engineering (c-RISE) at Memorial University of Newfoundland, Canada. During this period, he conducted research on LNG spill dispersion and its impact modellings, which were published in peer-reviewed journals. Prior to moving to Tasmania, from 2006- 2009 he served as a Mathematics and Science teacher at Saraswati Secondary English Boarding School in Dhanusha, Nepal. In this role, he taught Mathematics and Science to grades 8, 9, and 10, managed and conducted student examinations, and worked as a facility manager in the science laboratory.Dr. Baalisampang's contributions have been recognised through several awards and grants, including the Rob Lewis Award for Excellence in Postgraduate Research (2020), the Young Gastech Award (2017) and a Teaching Merit Certificate (2023). He is a member of prestigious organizations such as the American Society of Mechanical Engineers, Engineers Australia, and the Golden Key International Honour Society. Dr. Baalisampang actively contributes to the academic community as a reviewer for several high-impact journals in his field. Dr. Til Baalisampang is a dedicated academic and researcher with a strong background in maritime systems and safety engineering. His experience, coupled with his passion for teaching and research, positions him as a significant contributor to the field and a valuable asset to the Australian Maritime College and the broader engineering community."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Til Baalisampang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Til.Baalisampang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Til.Baalisampang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Til.Baalisampang@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
