<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-vinh-to-a108ba740381> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Vinh To"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/faculty-of-education-7cf8fd76e8d1> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Vinh To is a Senior Lecturer in English Curriculum and Pedagogy and a Graduate Research Coordinator in the School of Education, Arts and Society, at the University of Tasmania, Australia. Her research interest includes educational linguistics, English, literacy and languages education, and online education. Dr To is Founder of the Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest Group (SFLIG) and lead chief investigator of the Australia-ASEAN Academics Forum: Online Education during COVID-19 and beyond (AAAF), funded by the Australian Government’s Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade. She is the lead Convenor of SFLIG Conferences and AAAF Webinars, and Editor of SFLIG books and special issues. Dr To is the sole, lead and co-writer of a number of journal articles, book chapters, and media stories. She has published in top journals such as Australian Journal of Linguistics, Australian Journal of Language and Literacy, English in Australia, International Journal of Early Years Education, Linguistics and Human Sciences, and in highly regarded books with reputable publishers such as Springer Nature and Cambridge University Press. Her research activities appear in media news across the Australian and ASEAN regions. Dr To has been invited to deliver international keynote and plenary speeches in Vietnam, Lithuania, Spain, Indonesia and Italy. She has been awarded a Commendation for Research Innovation and Impact, and a number of teaching awards such as Teaching Merit Certificates, Deputy Vice-Chancellor's Commendation Letter, Certificate for Citation for Oustanding Contributions to Student Learning, Vice-Chancellor's Teaching Innovation Award in recognition of her excellent teaching in blended learning or fully online courses at the University of Tasmania. Career summaryBefore joining the University of Tasmania, Vinh was a full time English Language Lecturer in a university in Vietnam for five years. She taught general English, English for academic and specific purposes. She also supervised undergraduate research projects and contributed to curriculum design and development. Before working full time in a university in Vietnam, Vinh worked as a part-time English language teacher at various foreign language centres, and as a full time HR and administration officer in a company for two years. Vinh joined the University of Tasmania in 2012 as a PhD candidate and completed her PhD in 2015. Vinh worked as a casual academic in various positions from January 2014 to May 2016. In June 2016, Vinh accepted her full time academic position at the University of Tasmania.QualificationsPhD (2015) 'Linguistic complexity in English textbooks: A functional grammar perspective', University of TasmaniaGradCert (2015), University of TasmaniaCert (IDELT) (2015), Australian National UniversityMA (Applied Linguistics) (2009), University of DanangBA (English Education) (2005), University of DanangLanguages (other than English)Vietnamese (mother tongue)French (second language learner)Chinese (second language learner)Professional Positions Dr To is the Founder of the Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest Group (SFLIG) and leading organiser of the SFLIG Webinars and Conferences. She is also the co-founder of the Australia-ASEAN Academics Forum (AAAF): Online Education During COVID-19 and Beyond and leading organiser of the AAAF webinars. Founder/Convenor/ Lead Administrator, Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest GroupFounder/Convenor/ Lead Administrator, the Australia-ASEAN Academics Forum: Online Education During COVID-19 and beyond Lead Convenor, the Third International Online Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest Group Conference (SFLIG 2025)Lead Convenor, the Second International Online Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest Group Conference (SFLIG 2023)Lead Convenor, the First International Online Systemic Functional Linguistics Interest Group Conference (SFLIG 2021)Sole Convenor, International Systemic Functional Linguistics Webinars (SFLIG 2020) Lead Convenor, Australia-ASEAN Academics Forum (AAAF 2023) Lead Convenor, Australia-ASEAN Academics Forum (AAAF 2021) Guest Editor, Linguistics and the Human Sciences (2021- present) Guest Editor, Language, context and text: The social semiotics forum (LANGCT) (2026) Associate Editor, Australian Journal of Language and Literacy (2026) Co-Editor, ALEA Literacy Learning: The Middle Years (2022-2023)Associate Editor, ALEA Literacy Learning: The Middle Years (2020-2022)Associate Editor - Copy Chief, Australian Journal of Language and Literacy (2021) Co-Organiser, SFL Day, ALEA National Conference in Fremantle (2026)Co-Organiser: Teacher Educators’ Day, ALEA National Conference in Melbourne (2019)Co-Administrator, ALEA Literacy Teacher Educators’ Special Interest Group (2019-2020)Committee Member, Australian Literacy Educators' Association (ALEA), Tasmania North (2016-2019)"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Vinh To"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Vinh.To"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Vinh.To"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Vinh.To@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
