<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/professor-jason-smith-00676985e02a> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Professor Jason Smith"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-natural-sciences-7ce3a3316721> ;
    utas:bio "Jason A Smith is a Professor in Chemistry and carries out research in the area of Organic Chemistry, designing and synthesising new molecules for Drug Discovery. He studies the role of organic molecules in living systems, such as determining the role of plant hormones and drug development and metabolism. Organic Chemistry plays a major role in improving society by developing new drugs to combat disease and understanding chemical processes for the production of commodity chemical from renewable feedstocks.BiographyJason is a graduate of Flinders University of South Australia where he obtained both his BSc (Hons) and PhD. He has carried out post-doctoral research at Texas A&M (with Nobel Laureate Prof Sir Derek HR Barton) and at Australian National University (Prof Martin Banwell). In 1999 he received an AMRAD postdoctoral award and the RACI Athel Beckwith Lectureship in 2005.Career summaryQualifications PhD: Flinders University (1997) BSc (Hons): Flinders University (1993) BSc: Flinders University (1992)MembershipsCommittee associations Fellow of the Royal Australian Chemical Institute"^^xsd:string ;
