<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/professor-xiaolin-wang-1fefbb8f057b> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Professor Xiaolin Wang"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-engineering-757090ead0c4> ;
    utas:bio "Professor Wang has an internationally recognised research profile in thermodynamics, cooling engineering, desalination, energy storage and conversion, battery thermal management, and renewable energy utilization. He is a Fellow of Engineers Australia and a member of the World Society of Sustainable Energy Technologies. He received the DAAD Visiting Scholar from the German Academic Exchange Service in 2003 and the Ludwig Mond Prize from the Institution of Mechanical Engineers (IMechE), United Kingdom, in 2005. He was selected for the Australia–China Young Scientist Exchange Program (2009) and the Australia–Japan Emerging Research Leader Program (2016) by the Australian Academy of Technological Sciences and Engineering. He received the Dean’s Award for Outstanding Research Performance (2016) and the UTAS College Award for Research Excellence (2023) from the University of Tasmania. He has been recognised as a Field Leader in Thermal Sciences by The Australian Research Magazine in 2018 and 2026, and has been listed among the Stanford/Elsevier Top 2% Scientists since 2021. In 2024, he received the Applied Thermal Engineering Editors' Choice Award. He currently serves as Subject Editor for Applied Thermal Engineering and Associate Editor for Scientific Reports and Proceedings of the Institution of Mechanical Engineers, Part E: Journal of Process Mechanical Engineering. He has also served as a Guest Editor for Applied Sciences and Energies, and is a board member of five other international journals. BiographyProfessor Wang received his B.Eng and Ph.D. degrees from the Xi'an Jiaotong University, China in 1994 and 1999, respectively. After he worked in the industry in Singapore for three years, he started his academic career as a Research Fellow (A) in the Department of Mechanical Engineering, the National University of Singapore in 2002. In 2003, he was invited by DAAD, Germany to work as a visiting scientist at the University of Siegen, Germany. In 2005, he joined the School of Mechanical and Chemical Engineering, the University of Western Australia as a Lecturer and was promoted to Research Associate Professor in 2009. In July 2012, he joined the School of Engineering, University of Tasmania. Xiaolin has extensive industrial experiences in thermodynamics of cooling and power systems, heat pump technologies, desalination, energy storage and conversion, and renewable energy applications. He is Deputy Director of the Centre for Renewable Energy and Power Systems in the School of Engineering.Career summaryQualificationsPhD Xi'an Jiaotong University China BEng Xi'an Jiaotong University ChinaLanguages (other than English)Chinese Awards and Honours 2026 Field Leader in Thermal Sciences by the Australian Research Magazine. 2024: Editors' Choice Award (Applied Thermal Engineering). 2023: College Award: Research Excellence, Finalist for the Vice-Chancellor Award.2018: Field Leader in Thermal Sciences by the Australian Research Magazine.2016: Dean's Award by UTAS SET Faculty.2016: Australia Japan Emerging Research Leader Exchange Program award by the Australian Academy of Technological Science and Engineering (ATSE).2011: Recipient of the Australia-China Young Scientist (ACYS) exchange next step fund by the Australian Academy of Technological Science and Engineering (ATSE).2010: One of seven alumni representatives of ACYS shanghai summit awarded by ATSE.2009: One of eight representatives of ACYS exchange program awarded by ATSE.2005: Ludwig Mond Prize 2005, Process Industries Division Prizes awarded by IMechE of United Kingdom.2003: Visiting Scholar awarded by DAAD, Germany."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Professor Xiaolin Wang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Xiaolin.Wang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Xiaolin.Wang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Xiaolin.Wang@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/electrical-energy-storage-40c8e8ccf533>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/electrical-engineering-d4636d6bff5f>,
