<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/associate-professor-kathleen-beyer-60984ce208c0> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Associate Professor Kathleen Beyer"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-geography-planning-and-spatial-sciences-de1e76643cc9> ;
    utas:bio "Kathleen is a climate impacts and adaptation scientist with over 15 years’ experience working across government, academia, and the applied science sector. She is Director of the Climate Futures research group at the University of Tasmania and Associate Professor in Climate Impacts and Adaptation in the School of Geography, Planning and Spatial Sciences. Her work centres on delivering high-resolution regional climate information and decision-ready tools that help communities, industries, and governments plan for a changing climate. At the heart of her research is the connection between science, people, and policy—turning complex climate data into practical solutions for sectors ranging from health and infrastructure to water, energy, and biodiversity. She has led major initiatives including the NARCliM regional climate projections and the Natural Hazards research program for New South Wales. Kathleen currently leads the Natural Hazards Atlas for Tasmania and the new Regionally downscaled climate projections for Tasmania, which are shaping climate resilience strategies across the state. With a background spanning biosecurity, ecological modelling, aquatic ecosystem restoration and environmental policy, Kathleen takes a systems-level approach to adaptation, combining scientific rigour with local relevance. She is passionate about building climate literacy, co-designing adaptation strategies with stakeholders, and mentoring the next generation of climate experts. Kathleen also serves on national committees and advisory panels, helping to shape climate change leadership in Australia."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Associate Professor Kathleen Beyer"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Kathleen.Beyer"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Kathleen.Beyer"^^xsd:string ;
