<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-ashley-dyson-2901cbb43a67> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Ashley Dyson"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Ashley Dyson is a lecturer in civil and geotechnical engineering at the University of Tasmania’s School of Engineering. Ashley has established a reputation for strong industry-aligned geotechnical engineering research, with contributions to computational and probabilistic geotechnics, particularly in the fields of slope stability, landslides and offshore engineering. His research seeks to benefit the local Tasmanian community, with a focus on debris flow and landslide risk mitigation measures, as well as offshore foundation systems for Tasmanian renewable energy and aquaculture projects. Ashley currently serves on the ISSMGE technical committee TC304 (Engineering Practice of Risk Assessment and Management) and the Tasmanian division committee of Engineers Australia."^^xsd:string ;
