<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-chen-zhao-26a8a029cac3> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Chen Zhao"@en ;
    utas:bio "I am an ARC DECRA Fellow and ice sheet modeller at IMAS. I am interested in exploring the sea-level contributions from the Antarctic Ice Sheet in a changing climate and assessing how large ice sheets respond to evolving climate and ocean conditions through numerical modelling. My expertise includes ice sheet and coupled ice sheet–ocean modelling, ice dynamics and basal processes, subglacial hydrology, ice–ocean interactions, and sea-level rise. I am also interested in applying artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning techniques to advance cryospheric research, particularly for improving model performance, data integration, and predictive understanding of ice-sheet behaviour.Involvement in international projects:MISOMIP1: the first phase of the Marine Ice Sheet–Ocean Model Intercomparison Project ISMIP6: Ice Sheet Model Intercomparison Project for CMIP6Memberships:European Geosciences Union IUGG International Association of Cryospheric Sciences The Australian Meteorological and Oceanographic Society (AMOS) Scientific Communities: Australian Centre for Excellence in Antarctic Science (ACEAS), Chief Investigator Australian Antarctic Program Partnership (AAPP) , Affilicated Investigator Clim2Ant project, The Research Council of Norway, Co-leader of WP3 Ice to Islands Project, DFAT, UTAS project contact, Investigator Committee Memberships:SCAR Rings Action Group (ICE SHEET MARGIN) SCAR Groundwater Action GroupACCESS-NRI Cryosphere Modelling Working Group (co-chair) Awards: 2025 Rising Star (Academic) Award under Women of Color in STEM Awards, STEM Sisters 2025 Tasmania’s Young Tall Poppy of the Year 2024 Tasmanian STEM Early Career Researcher of the Year 2024 UTAS College of Sciences and Engineering ECR Award2024 The J G Russell Award, Australian Academy of Science 2024 ARC DECRA Award 2022 The Richardson Medal as part of ISMIP6 community, International Glaciological Society2019 Chinese Government Award for Outstanding Students AbroadResearch Grant: 2024-2025 Sea-level rise fingerprinting projects, Australian-French Association for Research and Innovation, $6,0002024-2026 DECRA Fellowship, Chief Investigator, Australian Research Council, $444,0002024-2027 Researcher Project for Scientific Renewal, Co-leader of working package 3, The Research Council of Norway, $1,447,0002021-2025 National Computing Merit Allocation Scheme, Chief investigator, National Computing Infrastructure, total 52,000 kSU computing resources ($2080,000 in-kind value)"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Chen Zhao"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Chen.Zhao"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Chen.Zhao"^^xsd:string ;
