<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-muhammad-bilal-amin-578e3bd82dc9> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Muhammad Bilal Amin"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-information-and-communication-technology-bb00fdcb9d1d> ;
    utas:bio "Dr. Bilal is a Senior Lecturer at the College of Science and Engineering, UTas. His research interests lie in the fields of software architecture, distributed systems, and data platforms.With a background in the software industry, Dr. Bilal brings valuable industry experience to his academic role. Before obtaining his PhD, he worked in the United States, designing and developing software systems ranging from medium- to enterprise-level for Fortune-500 companies. His industry experience involved utilising various programming languages, frameworks, and platforms for problem-solving. This experience greatly contributes to his success as an academic, teaching software development courses, and his achievements as a researcher. Dr. Bilal's efforts have been recognised by both industry and academia. His research proposals have been accepted by esteemed organisations such as Microsoft Research, Lockheed Martin Australia, EU Asia Connect, and the National Research Foundation of Korea. The impact and potential of his work are evident in his publications in top-tier journals and his patents held in the United States, Japan, and South Korea.The pinnacle of Dr. Bilal's research career came in 2016 when he was awarded the prestigious Korea Research Fellowship by the National Research Foundation (NRF) and South Korea's Ministry of Science and ICT. This highly competitive international fellowship, with an acceptance rate of less than 5%, is open to researchers from all fields of science and technology. Additionally, Dr. Bilal was recognised as an outstanding overseas researcher for the year 2017 by the NRF.Throughout his industry and academic career, Dr. Bilal has collaborated with colleagues from diverse cultures and traditions, spanning across Australia, South Korea, the United States, and Pakistan. He has found that these diverse partnerships often lead to the most innovative research.Before joining the University of Tasmania, Dr. Bilal served as a Korea Research Fellow and Research Professor at Kyung Hee University in South Korea.Career summaryQualificationsPhD Multi-dimensional Performance-based Ontology Matching over Cloud Platforms Kyung Hee University South Korea Aug-2015MS. DePaul University Chicago USA June-2006Languages (other than English) Urdu, PanjabiMembershipsOther*Australian Computing Society (ACS)Administrative expertiseBilal has successfully led several large-scale research projects in his academic career. The most prominent one is the project Mining Minds, which is a cloud-based wellness platform. Under his technical and management leadership, this project was completed by a team of 15 PhD and MS students. Upon completion, the project received an acceptance ratio above 90% and was highly regarded for its innovation."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Muhammad Bilal Amin"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Bilal.Amin"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Bilal.Amin"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Bilal.Amin@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/artificial-intelligence-803b3eb2b6af>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/artificial-intelligence-not-elsewhere-classified-2be812b5b6a8>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/distributed-computing-and-systems-software-c00bbe295243>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/distributed-computing-and-systems-software-not-elsewhere-classified-9b516a017370>,
