<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-rachel-climie-79ba2a2fc386> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Rachel Climie"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/menzies-institute-for-medical-research-12e6f452c508> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Rachel Climie is an NHMRC Emerging Leader, Heart Foundation Future Leader Fellow and Clinical Exercise Physiologist. Rachel's research is focused on primordial prevention (the prevention of risk factor onset) of cardiovascular disease, commencing in early life. Rachel and her team are developing ways to identify young people at risk of premature heart disease and working with local communities to develop solutions to minimise this risk. Rachel completed her PhD at the Menzies Institute for Medical Research in 2016. She then undertook 2 years postdoctoral research studying cardiovascular epidemiology and arterial mechanics at Paris Research Center Cardiovasculaire (PARCC), France, where she is an Honorary Fellow. Rachel was awarded a Heart Foundation Postdoctoral Fellowship (and Paul Korner Award) to work with the Sports Cardiology research team at the Baker Heart and Diabetes Institute, before returning to Tasmania in 2021. Rachel established and leads the Youth Vascular Consortium, a large international Consortium to investigate blood vessel ageing (vascular ageing) in young people. She is the co-lead a European network \"Primordial Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease and beyond in Europe\"; Chair of the Knowledge Exchange Working Group on the European Artery Society/VascAgeNet, Chair of Advocacy and Society Liaison on the Hypertension Australia Board and on the Public Health Association of Australia Tasmanian Branch Committee. Rachel is a past member of the Australian Cardiovascular Alliance Emerging Leaders Committee and past HBPRCA ECR Committee Chair. Rachel was awarded a Victorian Young Tall Poppy award in 2020 in recognition of her research."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Rachel Climie"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Rachel.Climie"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Rachel.Climie"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "Rachel.Climie@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:hasResearchField <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/biomedical-and-clinical-sciences-dd47e129275f>,
        <https://example.org/utas-research/research_field/cardiology-incl-cardiovascular-diseases-e160644219c4>,
