<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-reza-emad-f86358257286> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Reza Emad"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/australian-maritime-college-b2b959211c61> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Reza Emad started his career in the maritime industry as a seafarer. Since he received his MSc in Maritime Education and Training from World Maritime University in 1993 he pursued his passion as a maritime lecturer and researcher in competency development of seafaring and human factors in ports and shipping. He obtained his PhD from the University of Victoria, Canada in 2011. In his academic career, apart from teaching and research, he has held senior administrative positions including Head of Department and Academic Dean. He joined the Australian Maritime College in February 2016 as a Senior Lecturer and researcher. In 2017 he held the position of AMC Post Graduate Course Coordinator. In 2021 he founded and is directing the C-HELM (Centre for Research in Cognitive Human Element in the Maritime Domain). Professional Qualification:Watchkeeping Certificate of Competency (Deck-Unlimited)Professional memberships: Engineers Australia - Australasian Association for Engineering Education Australian Academic Integrity Network (AAIN) The Society for Nautical Research Association of Naval Architects and Marine Engineers Committee membership: 2021 – to date: University of Tasmania Human Research Ethics Committee 2021 – to date: University of Tasmania Industry 4.0 Community of Practice 2020 – to date: Academic Integrity Appeals Panel member, College of Science and Engineering, University of Tasmania 2020 – 2021: Research Committee elected member, Australian Maritime College 2016 – 2021: Learning and Teaching Committee member, Australian Maritime College 2017 – 2019: Learning and Teaching Committee member, College of Science and Engineering, University of TasmaniaEditorial Board Membership: Global Advanced Research Journal of Educational Research and Review Journal of Advances in Higher Education International Journal of Vocational Education and Training Research Maritime Research and Technology (MRT) Journal"^^xsd:string ;
