<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-shuxiang-xu-0911324db5ab> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Shuxiang Xu"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Shuxiang Xu is a Lecturer within the School of Information & Communication Technology, College of Sciences and Engineering, University of Tasmania, Tasmania, Australia. His research interests are Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Deep Learning, and Data Mining. Much of his work is focused on developing new Machine Learning or Deep Learning algorithms and using them to solve problems in various application fields such as Computer Vision and Natural Language Processing. He has taught in the fields of Artificial Intelligence, Operating Systems, Computer Networks, and Programming and Software Development.Shuxiang is a registered supervisor for PhD students and Master by Research students. If you are interested in studying for a research degree (PhD or Master by Research), please contact Shuxiang via Shuxiang.Xu@utas.edu.au.MembershipsMember of the Australian Computer Society (ACS)"^^xsd:string ;
