<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-soonja-yeom-d898cb9b3972> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Soonja Yeom"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-information-and-communication-technology-bb00fdcb9d1d> ;
    utas:bio "Dr. Soonja Yeom has been an academic staff member at the University of Tasmania’s School of ICT since 1994. She has taken a leadership role by working as the course coordinator for numerous courses within the School. Soonja’s dedication to enhancing the learning experience for students has earned her considerable recognition throughout her academic career. This commitment has led her to concentrate her research on leveraging technology for improved learning experiences and outcomes. Soonja's research expertise encompasses several domains, including Educational Technology, Learning Analytics, Affective Computing, Cybersecurity, and Authentication. Soonja has a substantial publication record, over 100 published works, and actively contributes to editing journals. She currently serves as the Chief Editor for two Special Issues in Education Sciences: “Technology-Enhanced Learning in Tertiary Education,\" and \"Cybersecurity and Online Learning in Tertiary Education.” Dr. Yeom has been honoured with numerous teaching awards over the years, including two Vice Chancellor's Citations for Outstanding Contributions to Student Learning in 2024. Some of her recent awards, Teaching Merit Certificates include recognition for Student Support of Learning in 2019, Teaching Group-Based Projects with Industry Clients in 2020, and Student-Centered Learning and Teaching Practice in 2021. As the course coordinator for the Master of Information Technology and Systems (MITS), Dr. Yeom led a successful course transformation in 2021 and led two MITS course accreditations, demonstrating her administrative capacity. Soonja also served as Course Coordinator for the Bachelor of Computing, Graduate Diploma of Computing, and Master of Computing from 1994 to 2013. Soonja actively contributes to the global academic community through her longstanding involvement with the UNESCO International Federation for Information Processing (IFIP). She has been a member of IFIP Working Group 3.3 – Research into Educational Applications of Information Technology since 2015. More recently, she became an inaugural member of IFIP Working Group 13.6 – Human Work Interaction Design (HWID) in 2024, and of Working Group 3.9 – Artificial Intelligence in Education in 2025. Soonja was recently featured in the Women in Technology poster series. Readers are encouraged to print them and put them up in corridors to encourage more girls to seek STEM careers."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Soonja Yeom"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Soonja.Yeom"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Soonja.Yeom"^^xsd:string ;
