<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/doctor-wenli-yang-a10946937c50> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Doctor Wenli Yang"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/school-of-information-and-communication-technology-bb00fdcb9d1d> ;
    utas:bio "Dr Wenli Yang is a Lecturer in the School of Information and Communication Technology at the University of Tasmania. She holds two PhDs—one in System Analysis and Integration from Huazhong University of Science and Technology (2012) and another in Computer Engineering from the University of Tasmania (2022). Her career spans across China, the United States, and Australia, with experience in both academic and industry roles. Before joining UTAS in 2017, she worked as a research scholar at the University of California, Davis, and spent five years as an associate telecommunications engineer focusing on intelligent transport systems. Her transition from industry to academia, supported by dual doctoral qualifications, highlights a unique and productive research trajectory shaped by real-world challenges and technical depth. Dr Yang has extensive experience in applied AI research and leadership, with a strong record of success in both academic and industry-linked projects. Her research spans image processing, machine learning and deep learning, knowledge representation and reasoning, explainable AI, and generative AI. She focuses on building AI models that are robust, scalable, and adaptable, designed to operate reliably across varied data sources and real-world conditions. Dr Yang has strong experience working with government, academic, and industry partners. She collaborates with organisations such as the Australian Antarctic Data Centre, CSIRO, Australian Seafood Industries, Tasmanian Fisheries, and Nocturnal Wildlife Research, among others. These partnerships support cross-disciplinary research and have led to the development of AI-driven systems for areas including marine monitoring, aquaculture automation, environmental sensing, and Antarctic data integration. Dr Yang teaches across undergraduate, Honours, and postgraduate levels, coordinating units in artificial intelligence, data science, and research methods. Her teaching approach blends real-world tools, industry engagement, and experiential learning. She has developed innovative and industry-aligned materials, receiving consistently positive feedback. Her experience includes unit coordination, material development, and the integration of authentic assessments that reflect professional practice for applied technologies. Dr Yang serves as the Honours Coordinator. In this role, she supports honour and master research pathway students in navigating their academic journeys and fosters a positive and inclusive environment for their professional development. She actively mentors students at all stages of their research journey, helping them explore supervisors, identify suitable topics, navigate proposal development, and connect with interdisciplinary opportunities."^^xsd:string ;
    utas:canonicalName "Doctor Wenli Yang"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileId "Yang.Wenli"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:discoveryProfileUrl "https://discover.utas.edu.au/api/users/Yang.Wenli"^^xsd:string ;
    utas:email "yang.wenli@utas.edu.au"^^xsd:string ;
