<https://example.org/utas-research/supervisor/professor-matt-king-d7689f9142c6> a utas:Supervisor ;
    rdfs:label "Professor Matt King"@en ;
    utas:affiliatedWith <https://example.org/utas-research/school/university-of-tasmania-aef6a7aa1611> ;
    utas:bio "I am a Laureate Fellow of the Australian Research Council and Professor of Polar Geodesy at the University of Tasmania, Australia. I also have the pleasure of being Director of the Australian Centre for Excellence in Antarctic Science (www.antarctic.org.au). My Laureate Fellowship focuses on tracking and predicting the future of the East Antarctic Ice Sheet. Starting from 2026, I will be building a team of about 12 postdocs and PhD students and working with a great team of collaborators in Australia and overseas. We will work on improving estimates of surface mass balance, observations of mass and elevation change, modelling and observing glacial isostatic adjustment, and ice sheet modelling. My background: After completing my PhD at the University of Tasmania in geodesy/glaciology I worked within one of Europe’s leading geodesy groups at the University of Newcastle upon Tyne from 2002-2012. During that time, I progressed from Junior Research Associate to Full Professor while working on problems within academia and industry. In late 2012, I returned to the University of Tasmania as Professor of Polar Geodesy. Through my career I have been supported by competitive research fellowships (NERC Postdoctoral Fellowship, RCUK Academic Fellowship, ARC Future Fellowship, and now ARC Laureate Fellowship).During my career, I have been able to work with outstanding colleagues from across geodesy, glaciology, solid Earth sciences, oceanography and many other fields. I have received a number of prestigious prizes and fellowships, including from the Royal Society of London and the Australian Academy of Sciences.Collaboration:I’ve been blessed to work with some wonderful early (and senior!) career researchers from many countries, including a great group of PhD students and postdocs. We work in a collaborative way to try and tackle problems that are of importance to populations globally. Our work covers making original observations (such as in Antarctica), analysis of observations, and building models to explain these.Memberships:American Geophysical Union, European Geosciences Union, Royal Society of Tasmania Awards/Prizes/Keynote Lectures 2025 Plenary Lecture, International Federation of Surveyors (FIG) Working Week, Australia 2022 Tasmanian STEM Researcher of the Year 2018 Mawson Medal and Lecture, Australian Academy of Science 2018 Keynote Lecture, The New Zealand Institute of Surveyors and Spatial Conference 2017 S.T. Lee Lecture, Victoria University of Wellington, New Zealand. 2016 M.R. Banks Medal, The Royal Society of Tasmania 2015 Vice Chancellor’s Award for Internationally Recognised Research 2015 Dean’s Award for Research Excellence 2015 Elected Fellow of the International Association of Geodesy 2015 Royal Society (London) Kavli Medal and Lecture 2015 Outstanding Reviewer, Earth and Planetary Science Letters 2013 Scopus Young Researcher Award Finalist 2012 American Geophysical Union Geodesy Section Prize 2012 Bullerwell Lecture (British Geophysical Association, European Geosciences Union) 2009 Philip Leverhulme Prize Prestigious Fellowships: I have been awarded four competitive research fellowshipsNERC postdoctoral fellowship (one of ~30 awarded per year; 2006-2009)Research Councils UK Academic Fellowship (2009-2012)ARC Future Fellowship (2012-2016) ARC Laureate Fellowship (2026-2031)Chair of Committees: 2025-2026 Chair, AGU Geodesy Section Honors Search Committee 2016-2020 Australian Council Delegate, International Union for Geodesy and Geophysics 2016-2020 Co-chair, Scientific Committee for Antarctic Research SERCE Research Program 2018-2020 Immediate Past President, The Royal Society of Tasmania 2016-2018 President, The Royal Society of Tasmania 2016-2017 Leader, Internationalisation Program, School of Land and Food 2014-2018 Theme Leader, Antarctic Gateway Partnership 2011-2016 Chair/Co-Chair, IAG Sub-Commission 3.4: Cryospheric Deformation 2010-2012 Chair of UK NERC Space Geodesy Facilities Steering Committee 2010 Chair, International GNSS Service Workshop Local Organising Committee 2009-2010 Chair, AGU Fall Assembly Geodesy Program 2008-2012 Chair, COST Action ES0701 Committee Memberships: 2025-present Antarctica InSync Australian Steering Committee 2025 External PhD Examiner Delft University of Technology, The Netherlands 2024-present Australian Research Council College of Experts 2024 Promotions assessor, University of the Sunshine Coast, Australia 2024 External PhD Examiner Victoria University of Wellington, NZ 2023-2025 AGU Geodesy Section Honors Search Committee 2023 External PhD Examiner Nottingham University, UK 2023-2027 Australian Academy of Science Mawson Medal and Lecture Award Committee 2022 Promotions assessor, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, USA 2022 Professorial promotions assessments Nanyang Technological University, Singapore; University of Southampton, UK 2021 Review Committee for the Menzies Medical Research Institute 2020-present Geodesy Working Group, Intergovernmental Committee on Surveying and Mapping 2020-present External expert advisory board of EU PROTECT SLR project 2019 IPCC Special Report on Oceans and Cryosphere in a Changing Climate Expert Reviewer 2019 University Employee Onboarding Steering Committee 2018-present National Committee for Antarctic Research, Australian Academy of Science 2018-present University Promotions Committee 2018-2019 University Research Committee 2018 Selection Panel, Tasmanian STEM Communicator of the Year 2018 AuScope Independent Program Review 2018-2019 School Leadership Team, School of Technology, Environments and Design 2017-2021 Australian Council of Environmental Deans and Directors 2017 Promotions panel, Abdulaziz University, Saudi Arabia 2016-2019 Member, University of Tasmania Student Discipline Panel 2016-2017 Member, Senior Management Team, School of Land and Food 2014-2016 Discipline Research Leader, Geography and Spatial Sciences 2014-2019 NCRIS AuScope Infrastructure Reference Panel 2014 University ERA2015 submission committee 2014 External PhD Examiner ANU, Australia 2013 Expert Reviewer European Space Agency “The Changing Earth” 2013 Co-chair IAG Sub-commission 3.4 Workshop, Ilulissat, Greenland 2013 Professorial appointments panel Tallinen University of Technology, Estonia 2013 Promotions panel, NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory 2012 External PhD Examiner University of Berne, Switzerland 2012 External PhD Examiner University College London, UK 2012 IPCC AR5 Expert Reviewer 2011 11th International Symposium on Antarctic Earth Sciences Scientific Steering Committee 2010-2012 NERC Peer Review College 2010 External PhD Examiner Durham University, UK 2010 International GNSS Service Workshop Scientific Programme Committee 2009-2014 European Science Foundation Pool of Reviewers 2009-2014 DynaQlim Steering Committee 2009 Appointments panel, Lamont Doherty Earth Observatory of Columbia University 2007-2012 UK National Committee for Antarctic Research Editorial Roles: 2015- 2019, Journal of Geodesy2014- Editorial Advisory Board, Journal of Geodetic ScienceCo-Editor of Special Issue of Tectonophysics. “Observation and Modeling of Glacial Isostatic Adjustment”, 2010Editorial Board of International Association of Geodesy Symposia 2011, 2017Scientific Editor Annals of Glaciology, Volume 54, issue 64, 2013, “The geophysics of the cryosphere”"^^xsd:string ;
